{
  "arxiv_id": "2303.07109",
  "title": "Transformer-based World Models Are Happy With 100k Interactions",
  "methods": [
    {
      "method_name": "TWM",
      "is_own_method": true,
      "one_paragraph_description": "Transformer-based world model: observations are encoded by a CNN into stochastic discrete latent states; a Transformer-XL is applied autoregressively to the sequence of latent states, actions and rewards (three modalities as separate tokens) with history length 16 to compute a deterministic hidden state from which next latent, reward and discount are predicted. An actor-critic is trained purely on imagined trajectories (horizon 15, batch 400) starting from real latents; the policy input is only the latent state z. A balanced dataset-sampling procedure (temperature 20) selects starting points; the actor uses an entropy-threshold regularizer.",
      "conventional_lineage_hint": "'Our transformer-based world model (TWM) generates meaningful, new experience, which is used to train a policy that outperforms previous model-free and model-based reinforcement learning algorithms' (Abstract); Table 1 groups TWM under 'Imagination' — model-based RL / world models",
